# Unified paper-trading runtime dependencies, isolated from the weather/API stack.
#
# Alpaca's own SDK is used directly rather than a broker framework. The project
# already owns its broker abstraction -- backend/trading/domain.py (typed
# contracts), risk.py (deterministic risk gate), ledger.py (append-only audit),
# service.py (execution orchestration) and adapters/base.py (broker protocol) --
# so a second abstraction layer would be redundant. See
# docs/blockers/2026-08-28-lumibot-dependency.md for the measured comparison.
#
# The Alpaca adapter (backend/trading/adapters/alpaca_paper.py) takes an injected
# client factory, so this dependency is needed only for a real paper client at
# runtime; the entire test suite runs without it.
#
# ALWAYS compile against the application stack as a constraint, so the trading
# runtime can never silently upgrade or downgrade the app's pinned dependencies:
#   env -u PYTHONPATH "$ENVS/unified-trading-py311/bin/pip-compile" \
#       requirements-trading.in --constraint requirements.txt \
#       --constraint constraints-runtime.txt --output-file requirements-trading.txt
alpaca-py
